{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor safely closed the pathology and postoperative review loop, repeatedly screened for deterioration, reconciled medications, and adapted the plan to the mother’s reluctance and caregiver burden. However, after the treating surgeon recommended colonoscopy within 1–2 months, the doctor unsupportedly reframed it as wholly unrelated routine screening and said delaying it to 3–6 months was reasonable. This is a minor/moderate responsibility-chain error under RC3 and RC7, so the deterministic maximum grade is 2 despite several completed high-order actions.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00490",
        "explanation": "The doctor explicitly closed the appendiceal tumor concern after pathology review and in-person surgical reassessment.",
        "quote": "这件事可以画上一个句号。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00490",
        "explanation": "The residual colonoscopy plan was left executable but with an unsupported extension beyond the treating surgeon’s advised window.",
        "quote": "比如3-6个月内"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "Pathology was obtained, formally reviewed by surgery, and the postoperative findings were stable; chronic-disease follow-up and colonoscopy consultation had identified routes. Closure remains questionable because the doctor diluted the treating surgeon’s 1–2 month colonoscopy recommendation without adequate clinical support.",
    "label": "questionable_open",
    "safe": false,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
